# MkDocs-flavoured Markdown, which prettier does not speak. It DE-INDENTS
# admonition bodies (`!!! note` / `??? tip`), and MkDocs needs that indentation
# to associate the body with the box — so a correctly-written admonition came
# out rendering as an empty titled box with its text escaped into a paragraph
# below. 28 of the site's 30 admonitions were broken this way, because
# `format:check` is a CI gate: writing one correctly meant failing the gate.
# The content tabs (`=== "Python"`) and snippet includes (`--8<--`) survive only
# by luck. Formatting here is a human's job, not the formatter's.
docs-site/docs/
# The Material theme overrides (#401). Prettier's html parser does not speak
# Jinja, so it reflows tags across lines mid-statement (`{% include\n"…" %}`).
# That still runs, but it destroys the one property these files are maintained
# by: each is a fork of a partial shipped inside mkdocs-material, and the way a
# version bump gets reviewed is by diffing ours against theirs. A reformatted
# fork diffs against upstream on every line.
docs-site/overrides/
# Same rule again: the demo state sweep's three outputs are rendered by
# tools/gen_demo_state_map.py, whose --check gate compares them byte for byte
# against what python writes. Prettier collapses short arrays onto one line and
# python's json.dumps never does, so letting both format them would make the two
# gates contradict each other — one of them red whichever way a file is written.
landing/demo/state-map.json
landing/demo/divergence-notes.json
landing/demo/python-counts.json
